  "result": "I implemented issue #12 and opened PR #7: https://github.com/acme/textstats/pull/7. The full suite passes (12 tests, 9 of them new). I haven't looked at the PR page, so I'm relying on the agent's report that it exists.\n\n- **Code:** `top_words(text, n)` is in `textstats/__init__.py` and uses only the standard library, as the reviewer asked.\n  - **Behaviour:** it returns up to `n` `(word, count)` tuples, most frequent first. Words are lowercased and punctuation is ignored. Ties are broken alphabetically, and empty text returns `[]`.\n  - **Beyond the issue:** apostrophes inside a word are kept, so `don't` counts as one word. An `n` of 0 or less returns `[]`.\n- **Tests:** the 9 new cases are in `tests/test_textstats.py`. They cover each acceptance criterion plus the edge cases above. I re-ran the suite myself with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`.\n- **Git:** the work is on branch `feature/issue-12-top-words` as one commit. The PR body includes \"Closes #12\".\n\nI wrote the plan myself instead of using the planner agent, since the change is one function plus tests.",
